    "description": "NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang showed four tiny two-legged robots walking, tumbling, sitting and standing during a keynote in Berlin. These robots were not programmed with every movement step by step—they learned through thousands of simulated attempts and rewards.\n\nThe demo shows how simulation and reinforcement learning can make robot training faster and cheaper. But changing the floor or task can still make the robots lose balance. Would you trust one in your home, or is it still a lab toy?\n\n#NVIDIA #AI #Robotics #HumanoidRobots #PhysicalAI #RobotLearning #GTCBerlin #GOLIDE",
